{"parentUuid":"e485e75b-7b42-4320-96b5-440f2a68de99","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a99a44401cf927d52","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X4xje9rb94VuP9Tx2XEA2R","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EuroGP 2024 2025 hyper-heuristic constraint programming\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Genetic Programming as a Hyper-Heuristic for Solving ...\",\"url\":\"https://gecco-2025.sigevo.org/Tutorial?itemId=5127\"},{\"title\":\"EuroGP: European Conference on Genetic Programming 2026 2025 2024 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=960\"},{\"title\":\"EuroGP – EvoStar 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.evostar.org/2024/eurogp/\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"EuroGP – EvoStar 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.evostar.org/2025/eurogp/\"},{\"title\":\"European Conference on Genetic Programming (Part of EvoStar) | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/conference/eurogp\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon.com: Genetic Programming: 28th European Conference, EuroGP 2025, Held as Part of EvoStar 2025, Trieste, Italy, April 23–25, 2025, Proceedings (Lecture Notes in Computer Science): 9783031899904: Xue, Bing, Manzoni, Luca, Bakurov, Illya: Books\",\"url\":\"https://us.amazon.com/Genetic-Programming-European-Conference-Proceedings/dp/3031899903\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cp2024.a4cp.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic Programming: 27th European Conference, EuroGP 2024, Held as Part of EvoStar 2024, Aberystwyth, UK, April 3–5, 2024, Proceedings | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-56957-9\"},{\"title\":\"EvoCOP – EvoStar 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.evostar.org/2024/evocop/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about EuroGP 2024 and 2025:\n\n## EuroGP 2024\nEuroGP 2024 was the 27th European Conference on Genetic Programming, held in Aberystwyth, UK, April 3–5, 2024 and co-located with the EvoStar events, EvoCOP, EvoMUSART, and EvoApplications. The 13 papers (9 selected for long presentation and 4 for short presentation) were carefully reviewed and selected from 24 submissions. The papers covered topics including developing new variants of GP algorithms, as well as exploring GP applications to the optimization of machine learning methods and the evolution of control policies.\n\n## EuroGP 2025\nEuroGP 2025 is the 28th European Conference on Genetic Programming, held in Trieste, Italy, during April 23–25, 2025 and co-located with the EvoStar events, EvoCOP, EvoMUSART, and EvoApplications. Accepted papers are published by Springer Nature in the Lecture Notes in Computer Science series.\n\nRegarding the specific topic of **hyper-heuristic constraint programming**, the search results show a tutorial at GECCO 2025 on \"Genetic Programming as a Hyper-Heuristic\" but don't contain detailed information about hyper-heuristic constraint programming papers presented at EuroGP 2024 or 2025. You may want to check the official proceedings links to find specific papers on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d878dd1d-9439-4135-8f3e-b037782ddf40","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:46.150Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e485e75b-7b42-4320-96b5-440f2a68de99","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d9579e64-85e3-474e-a8d2-d0b699007002","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a99a44401cf927d52","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oz2tCuxTy9EX3E2uqnvLh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Genetic Programming SAT branching heuristic 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic Algorithm Based Solution to SAT-3 Problem\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.sciepub.com/jcsa/3/2/3/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Rank the Initial Branching Order of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.07176v1\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Learning Rate Based Branching Heuristic for SAT Solvers | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Learning-Rate-Based-Branching-Heuristic-for-SAT-Liang-Ganesh/c87744f74037b243da93c81720404177040f8854\"},{\"title\":\"Autonomous Code Evolution Meets NP-Completeness\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.07367v1\"},{\"title\":\"Search Strategy Generation for Branch and Bound Using Genetic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.09444v1\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring Hyper-heuristic Methodologies with Genetic Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-01799-5_6\"},{\"title\":\"Selecting the Best Lower-Bound Strategy in a Branch-and-Bound Algorithm Using Genetic Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-15455-2_4\"},{\"title\":\"ECADA - Bonsai Research Space\",\"url\":\"https://bonsai.auburn.edu/ecada/GECCO2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring Hyper-heuristic Methodologies with Genetic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://people.cs.nott.ac.uk/pszeo/docs/publications/ChapterGPasHH09.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant papers and research on genetic programming, SAT solvers, and branching heuristics from 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Research Highlights\n\n**Machine Learning and Neural Approaches to SAT Branching (2024-2025):**\n\nNeuroCore improves the branching heuristic for CDCL solvers by employing supervised learning to map UNSAT instances to their corresponding UNSAT core variables. Additionally, NeuroBack (Wang et al., 2024) adapts this strategy to conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL) solvers by predicting the initial phase (polarity).\n\n**Evolutionary Approaches to SAT Solving:**\n\nA particularly notable development is a family of self-evolved solver that outperforms the winning solvers of the SAT Competition 2025, using only five selected solvers from SAT 2024 as initial codebase. This work demonstrates that an AI agent based self-evolving coding framework can work at repository-level programming and compete at champion-level performance in NP-complete problem solving.\n\n**Genetic Programming for Search Strategies:**\n\nGP2S is evaluated on synthetic problem types for performance and generalizability, with heuristics generated from a subset of MIPLIB 2017 instances under a solving time limit and evaluated on the full dataset with extended time limits.\n\n**Learning-Based Branching Strategies:**\n\nGraph-Q-SAT and RDC-SAT use reinforcement learning to learn an optimal branching heuristic, with RDC-SAT polling a GNN every time a split is done in parallel SAT solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5422385d-8206-4195-9d48-10a22559762b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:47.444Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d9579e64-85e3-474e-a8d2-d0b699007002","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
