{"parentUuid":"11be9f1c-2fcf-4769-a8f2-168d0d262090","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a99a44401cf927d52","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvfxBnmmJyE78Aj4CuqHae","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PushGP lexicase selection 2024 2025 combinatorial optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Random subsampling improves performance in lexicase selection (Conference Paper) | NSF PAGES\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/biblio/10308964-random-subsampling-improves-performance-lexicase-selection\"},{\"title\":\"GP and LLMs for Program Synthesis: No Clear Winners\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.03966\"},{\"title\":\"Problem-solving benefits of down-sampled lexicase selection\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.06085\"},{\"title\":\"DALex: Lexicase-like Selection via Diverse AggregationSupported by Amherst College and members of the PUSH lab.\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2401.12424\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Uncompromising Problems with Lexicase Selection\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.hampshire.edu/lspector/pubs/lexicase-IEEE-TEC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"arXiv:2304.07089v2 [cs.NE] 1 Aug 2024\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.07089\"},{\"title\":\"Evolving Graphs with Cartesian Genetic Programming with Lexicase Selection | Proceedings of the Companion Conference on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3583133.3596402\"},{\"title\":\"Informed Down-Sampled Lexicase Selection: Identifying productive training cases for efficient problem solving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2301.01488\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Convergence with Lexicase Selection in Tree-Based Automated Machine Learning | Springer Nature Link (formerly SpringerLink)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-29573-7_11\"},{\"title\":\"[2301.01488v2] Informed Down-Sampled Lexicase Selection: Identifying productive training cases for efficient problem solving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.01488v2\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding PushGP, lexicase selection, and recent developments in 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Research on PushGP and Lexicase Selection\n\n### Informed Down-Sampled Lexicase Selection (2024)\n\nIn January 2024, research on genetic programming showed that random down-sampled lexicase selection evaluates individuals on only a random subset of training cases, allowing for more individuals to be explored with the same number of program executions. The work introduced Informed Down-Sampled Lexicase Selection, which leverages population statistics to build down-samples that contain more distinct and informative training cases. This method was investigated across two different GP systems including PushGP.\n\n### DALex: Diversely Aggregated Lexicase Selection (2024)\n\nDALex achieves significant speedups over lexicase selection and its relaxed variants while maintaining almost identical problem-solving performance on program synthesis, deep learning, symbolic regression, and learning classifier systems. DALex is up to 5x faster than lexicase selection.\n\n### Program Synthesis Benchmarking (2025)\n\nRecent improvements for PushGP have been attributed to the use of down-sampled lexicase, which has been shown to excel at program synthesis compared to other parent selection algorithms. Down-sampled lexicase demonstrated superior performance, solving 17 tasks on benchmark suites.\n\nThese developments show ongoing optimization efforts for PushGP in program synthesis tasks, with lexicase selection variants proving particularly effective for combinatorial optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"05ae6494-dcf4-4395-bbaa-bf7574fd2caa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:57.788Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11be9f1c-2fcf-4769-a8f2-168d0d262090","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"aa8fd56b-71cc-4ce2-92c1-148cdcd359c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a99a44401cf927d52","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C4rzdgGvD7rpi8H7K1xbtb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"hyper-heuristic genetic programming CP-SAT scheduling 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Genetic Programming-Based Hyper-Heuristic Algorithm for Dynamic Task Scheduling in Astronomical Observation Satellite | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-96-9901-8_35\"},{\"title\":\"Dual-tree genetic programming-based hyper-heuristic algorithm for dynamic task scheduling in astronomical observation satellite - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0273117725010920\"},{\"title\":\"A Self-Learning Hyper-Heuristic Algorithm Based on a Genetic Algorithm: A Case Study on Prefabricated Modular Cabin Unit Logistics Scheduling in a Cruise Ship Manufacturer - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11429851/\"},{\"title\":\"An effective Genetic Programming Hyper-Heuristic for ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.15070\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring Hyper-heuristic Methodologies with Genetic Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-01799-5_6\"},{\"title\":\"A cooperative coevolutionary genetic programming hyper-heuristic for multi-objective makespan and cost optimization in cloud workflow scheduling - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054824002776\"},{\"title\":\"An improved genetic programming hyper-heuristic for the dynamic flexible job shop scheduling problem with reconfigurable manufacturing cells - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S027861252400058X\"},{\"title\":\"[2602.15070] An effective Genetic Programming Hyper-Heuristic for Uncertain Agile Satellite Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.15070\"},{\"title\":\"Niching Genetic Programming based Hyper-heuristic Approach to Dynamic Job Shop Scheduling | Proceedings of the 2016 on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2908961.2908985\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic programming-based hyper-heuristic approach for solving dynamic job shop scheduling problem with extended technical precedence constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054821001672\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are relevant findings on hyper-heuristic genetic programming and CP-SAT scheduling research from 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Research Highlights\n\n**Genetic Programming Hyper-Heuristic Applications:**\n\nA Genetic Programming-Based Hyper-Heuristic Algorithm for Dynamic Task Scheduling in Astronomical Observation Satellite was published in 2025, demonstrating the application of GPHH to scheduling problems.\n\nA Dual-Tree Genetic Programming-based Hyper-Heuristic (DT-GPHH) algorithm was proposed for dynamic observation task scheduling, which evolves a pair of heuristics for task selection and time allocation within a task-driven dynamic scheduling simulator, using a novel dual-tree representation to enable simultaneous evolution of both heuristics.\n\n**2024-2025 Scheduling Research:**\n\nWei et al. (2024) successfully addressed the multi-objective dynamic scheduling problem of earth observation satellites by using a knowledge-transfer-based GP algorithm.\n\nAn improved Genetic Programming Hyper-Heuristic (GPHH) method was proposed to solve the dynamic flexible job shop scheduling problem considering reconfigurable manufacturing cells (DFJSP-RMCs) with completion time, delay time and reconfiguration time as optimization objectives.\n\nAn effective Genetic Programming Hyper-Heuristic (GPHH) was designed to automate the generation of scheduling policies, with evolved scheduling policies that can be utilized to adjust plans in real time and perform exceptionally well.\n\n**Note:** The search results do not contain specific information combining CP-SAT solver with hyper-heuristic genetic programming in the 2024-2025 timeframe.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c8dd981-c2fd-4632-8338-cd4ad9a1260a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:00.223Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aa8fd56b-71cc-4ce2-92c1-148cdcd359c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e9380e14-14d3-45ea-a66b-e9df565ee6af","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a99a44401cf927d52","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y7evvFTySzuQ2QiukndBfx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"genetic programming evolve cutting plane MIP 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EuroGP: European Conference on Genetic Programming 2026 2025 2024 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=960\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic Programming: 27th European Conference, EuroGP 2024, Held as Part of EvoStar 2024, Aberystwyth, UK, April 3–5, 2024, Proceedings | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-56957-9\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic Programming Theory and Practice XX (Genetic and Evolutionary Computation) [1st ed. 2024] 9819984122, 9789819984121 - DOKUMEN.PUB\",\"url\":\"https://dokumen.pub/genetic-programming-theory-and-practice-xx-genetic-and-evolutionary-computation-1st-ed-2024-9819984122-9789819984121.html\"},{\"title\":\"GI@ICSE 2025: 14th International Workshop\",\"url\":\"https://geneticimprovementofsoftware.com/events/papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Integer Programming Workshop 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/EUROMIP/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"EuroGP – EvoStar 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.evostar.org/2024/eurogp/\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Integer Programming Workshop 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Acknowledgment to reviewers (2024) | Genetic Programming and Evolvable Machines\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10710-025-09518-5\"},{\"title\":\"TPOT: Automating ML Pipelines with Genetic Algorithms in Python - KDnuggets\",\"url\":\"https://www.kdnuggets.com/tpot-automating-ml-pipelines-with-genetic-algorithms-in-python\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Integer Programming Society\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about genetic programming and MIP-related events and research, though I did not find a specific paper or research project directly combining all four elements (genetic programming, evolve, cutting plane, and MIP) together.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**Genetic Programming Conferences and Research:**\nThe 27th European Conference on Genetic Programming (EuroGP 2024) was held in Aberystwyth, UK in April 3-5, 2024, and the papers covered topics including developing new variants of GP algorithms, as well as exploring GP applications to the optimization of machine learning methods and the evolution of control policies.\n\n**Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) Research:**\nThe Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) Workshop is a single-track workshop highlighting the latest trends in integer programming and discrete optimization, with speakers chosen by invitation. The MIP Workshop 2025 will be held at the University of Minnesota.\n\n**Cutting Planes in MIP:**\nRecent work has proposed approaches that incrementally improve over current methods by using standard MIP techniques, like MIP starts and lazy constraint separation, and research has explored deriving bounds and cutting planes based on implications from solving scenario sub-problems, with computational findings demonstrating significant reductions in solution times.\n\nWhile these areas are active research domains, the search results did not reveal a specific paper or research project that explicitly combines genetic programming with cutting plane techniques for MIP problems in 2024-2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"95961a7a-9931-4864-aca7-a98bc2cf1f8c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:00.373Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e9380e14-14d3-45ea-a66b-e9df565ee6af","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"maste